01:02:30,000 --> 01:02:36,000
Sneakers is a 1992 American caper thriller film directed by Phil Alden Robinson
from a screenplay co-written with Walter Parkes and Lawrence Lasker.

13
01:07:42,500 --> 01:07:48,500
It stars Robert Redford, Dan Aykroyd, Ben Kingsley, Mary McDonnell,
River Phoenix, Sidney Poitier and David Strathairn.

14
01:12:55,000 --> 01:13:01,000
In the film, Martin (Redford) and his group of security specialists are hired to steal a
black box but soon realize the job has nefarious and far-reaching consequences.

15
01:18:07,500 --> 01:18:13,500
Lasker and Parkes first conceived Sneakers in 1981
during pre-production on WarGames (1983).

16
01:23:20,000 --> 01:23:26,000
Redford was the first actor attached to the project, and he helped
recruit the remaining cast members, as well as Robinson.

17
01:28:32,500 --> 01:28:38,500
Several of the characters were inspired by members of the hacking and national defense
communities, and the actors improvised several scenes during filming.

18
01:33:45,000 --> 01:33:51,000
Principal photography took place on location across California, with filming taking place in San
Francisco, Oakland, Simi Valley, and the Courthouse Square backlot at Universal Studios Hollywood.

19
01:38:57,500 --> 01:39:03,500
Sneakers was theatrically released in the United States on
September 11, 1992, by Universal Pictures.

20
01:44:10,000 --> 01:44:16,000
The film received generally positive reviews from critics,
with praise for its humor, tone, and plot.

21
01:49:22,500 --> 01:49:28,500
It grossed $105.2 million worldwide, becoming the
20th-highest-grossing film of 1992.

22
01:54:35,000 --> 01:54:41,000
The film explores themes of hacker, mathematician, assignment, calm, relaxed.

23
01:59:47,500 --> 01:59:53,500
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
